0..72 Comment "// Second-order rules. A rule whose right side applies a variable that a"
73..151 Comment "// binding port of its left side binds instantiates it: `t(u)` substitutes `u`"
152..228 Comment "// for the variable `t`\'s port binds, one argument per bound variable (Klop,"
229..307 Comment "// van Oostrom and van Raamsdonk, _Combinatory reduction systems: introduction"
308..379 Comment "// and survey_, TCS 121, 1993). The rules terminate by the higher-order"
380..458 Comment "// recursive path order (Jouannaud and Rubio, _The higher-order recursive path"
459..537 Comment "// ordering_, LICS 1999): the instantiation is below an application that holds"
538..615 Comment "// the variable and every argument directly. A pair a second-order rule takes"
616..689 Comment "// part in is found by pattern unification and joined in the second-order"
690..758 Comment "// reading (Mayr and Nipkow, _Higher-order rewrite systems and their"
759..790 Comment "// confluence_, TCS 192, 1998)."
792..868 Comment "/// ζ: `let` binds a term over its body, and its rule substitutes the bound"
869..892 Comment "/// term into the body."
